description:
PR group S1: one site PR with site-split-22 and site-split-24. Step 1 is done via gh api right after the site-split-20 push; everything after it goes in the S1 PR to main.

1. Settings:
   - Ruleset on main: require a PR, require the `ci` status check, squash only, linear history, block force pushes and deletion.
   - Environment `github-pages`: no required reviewers; deployment branch policy limited to `main`.
   - Pages build source "GitHub Actions", with no custom domain yet.
   - Variables: CORE_REPO=BenchBox-dev/BenchBox, SITE_ORIGIN=https://next.benchbox.dev, SITE_HOST=next.benchbox.dev. Leave SITE_DEPLOY_TARGET unset.
   - Confirm that the SITE_BRIDGE_APP_ID and SITE_BRIDGE_PRIVATE_KEY secrets exist (owner pre-work).
2. Write `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. They cover:
   - the no-Python rule;
   - bundle schema rules: integer major, N and N-1 support, core lands first;
   - the PR flow: named branch, squash, explicit-path staging, never `git add -A`;
   - commit identity Joe Harris <joeharris76@gmail.com>, with no agent trailers;
   - the comment policy: no explanatory comments in first-party code.
3. Tooling:
   - npm workspaces for website and explorer;
   - lefthook running markdownlint-cli2, cspell, a Node YAML lint and an agent-trailer commit-msg check;
   - a TS/Astro comment-policy check built from core's `scripts/comment_syntax_js.cjs`.
4. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, with every action pinned by SHA and a single `ci` aggregate job:
   - astro check, vitest, Explorer unit tests and Playwright e2e;
   - advisory visual regression against the deployed artifact (D8);
   - `npm audit --audit-level=high`;
   - an N and N-1 bundle-schema matrix using fixture bundles.
5. `.github/workflows/nightly.yml`:
   - the dependency audit;
   - lychee external links, which opens or updates one issue (D15);
   - an availability probe of every route class on SITE_ORIGIN, which opens one issue on failure. This replaces core's publication-canaries.
